title: '[pallet-revive] Serve the ETH RPC from inside the node'

doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    A `polkadot-omni-node` built with the experimental `experimental-eth-rpc-in-node` feature
    can serve the Ethereum JSON-RPC endpoint itself when started with `--eth-rpc`, replacing
    the separate `eth-rpc` process. It is configured with `--eth-rpc-port` (default 8545),
    `--eth-rpc-external`, `--eth-rpc-cors`, `--eth-rpc-pruning` and
    `--eth-rpc-allow-unprotected-txs`. The default `--eth-rpc-pruning archive` indexes the
    whole history into `<base-path>/chains/<chain id>/eth-rpc/eth-rpc.db` and needs an archive
    node for a complete sync; pass a number of blocks to keep only recent ones in memory. If
    the server fails, it logs an error and the node keeps running.

- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-revive-eth-rpc::client::connect` now returns only the `RpcClient`; build the subxt
    clients from it with the new `client::subxt_clients`:

    ```rust
    let rpc_client = connect(url, max_request_size, max_response_size).await?;
    let (api, rpc) = subxt_clients(rpc_client.clone()).await?;
    ```

    The crate's `experimental-eth-rpc-in-node` feature adds `in_process::start_embedded`,
    which serves the ETH RPC over a node's in-memory `RpcModule`. The subxt metadata is now
    checked in as `revive_chain.scale`, removing the build dependency on `revive-dev-runtime`;
    refresh it with `BLESS_METADATA=1`.

crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: major
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-omni-node
  bump: patch
